 easy steps",steps:[{title:"Fill in your details and verify your phone number",desc:"Provide your email and phone number and verify your phone number with an OTP.",img:"/personal/start-1.png"},{title:"Get verified",desc:"Select username & password. Provide your BVN and KYC details and start face & ID verification. You can then set up a PIN for managing your account.",img:"/personal/start-2.png"},{title:"Fund your accounts",desc:'Click on "add money" to find your account details, and top up to start making transfers',img:"/personal/start-3.png"},{title:"You're done!",desc:"Click on the Card menu to order a card and get it in 48hrs.",img:"/personal/start-4.png"}]},_=[{question:"What is personal banking?",answer:"Personal banking refers to financial services and products offered to individuals by a bank, including savings accounts, loans, and other services tailored for personal financial management."},{question:"What documents do I need to open a Moniepoint Personal Bank account?",answer:"To open an account, you only need a valid Nigerian phone number, a functional email address and your BVN. These will give you access to a functional bank account on KYC Level 1. Click here to learn more about the KYC levels."},{question:"Is there a fee for opening an account?",answer:"No, there is no fee for opening or maintaining an account with Moniepoint."},{question:"Is Moniepoint safe?",answer:"Yes! At Moniepoint, we take security seriously by implementing robust security measures to protect your financial information and transactions. We are also regulated by CBN and insured by NDIC."},{question:"Can a personal bank account be used for business?",answer:"We recommend that you have a separate personal bank account and business account to keep track of your finances properly."},{question:"How many personal bank accounts can I have?",answer:"You can have more than one personal bank account depending on your financial goal."},{question:"How do I access my account?",answer:"You can 